!! The loops ~ one line per open loop, beside the train that closes it

Each row names what stays owed, the train of #/the-trains that closes it, and who owes a ruling first
(''operator'', ''house'', or nobody). A row names its file so a builder reads the code before leaning on
the row; a line number drifts, so none rests here. Train letters: ''S'' the custody seal · ''G'' ground ·
''K'' the seat · ''N'' the Nexus founding act · ''P'' the Kahu plane · ''W'' the wire and the face proof ·
''E'' the ember · ''O1'' ONE FACE's sessions · ''H'' the hosted road ·
''A'' HARBOR's tail · ''V'' recovery's verbs · ''B'' the browser and the phones · ''X'' TWO HEARTHS.

!!! GROUND
* `G6` The evergreen sweep's remainder on held ground: stale prose, back-compat wording and tolerant readers in files other lanes hold, each named with its owner in the ground lane's shape file (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `nexus-seal-seed.ts`, `seed-wrap-prf.ts`, the tolerant readers in `ingest-core.ts`, `lar-uris.ts`, `mesh-palace.ts`); `cleanup-days.ts` stays unlocated. G; the false source comments ride the code lane of #/side-lanes.
* `G7` Custody's edges on train N's ground: a short seat can write a charter that boots torn (`nexus-seal.ts`); a floor-class carrier standing alone founds, which decides whether a new custody adopts a standing vessel key (identity ground); `setFoundingRoute` stands as a test seam in source (`found.ts`). N.
* `G8` Measures: the full-corpus per-verb flush re-measure; pack-PIN recursion; a production `assertBodyIndexTier` caller. G.
* `G10` The wiki shore's echo law: every leaked change routes as a save. Verify at the shore lane's close. G.
* `G13` Summons: no check of who wrote one; a consume tombstones every layer; dedup lives in memory (`verb-dispatcher.ts`, `verb-summons.ts`). Owed: a writer check, a working-layer tombstone alone, durable dedup, lease and fence, and honouring `aud`. House. G.
* `G15` The refold's answers. For the compose owner, who holds `open-node-vessel.ts`: `after-roll-awaited.test.ts` reads source shape alone, and wants the chain lifted into a module a vector can run; an unbounded `afterRollChain` stage can stall later rolls, and a bound must never let two refolds of one holder overlap. Beside those: the plugin build's transcript records a fixed logical path for the TW5 binary, never the resolved one (`build-plugin-tiddler.ts`); its cure moves genesis attestation bytes, so it rides a labelled re-bake. G.
* `G17` Tests only: the mutation survivors a closing review named; the sealed suite's coverage of each place the harness's root split changes behaviour. G.
* `G18` The shore: the mode row never moves. G or B.
* `G19` Canon sweeps owed: the shore surface's carriers; wherever the test door's "scratch" reads as a temp-dir test; the browser surface's secure-context law beside `docker-compose.mesh.yml`'s; `secure-context.mem#/behind-the-terminator` to harbor's law; `kahu.mem` and `lamplighters.mem` on what the code holds. G.
* `G20` Carried, unranked: road (iv), surface-for-review; loans keyed by CID; a design call on `/cas` timing; whether the parallel-draft alert persists; `packages/lararium-sensorium/requirements.txt` on the tree-sitter versions; one elyncia carrier that fails the corpus round-trip and wants an owner; the cold-boot `unavailable` reading of automerge-repo, where a widened grace wants the per-source map read first.
* `G27` A wiki island that stands live and unpinned takes no `lares shore` answer: the shore verb reaches the active wiki's island and the daemon island (`askShore`, `packages/lares-cli/src/shore-core.ts`), and a person settles a standoff in another live island by bringing the two sides to say the same. G.
