* `E4` The raise's commit point and its lapse (#/rulings, how a raise lapses; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>). Owed: the count spent at the raise ledger's durable commit, before SERVING composes, so a crash before the commit spends nothing and serves nothing and a crash after it burns the raise; and the raise's lapse at a lock, a restart, a human unlock or a counted removal, with no timer and no heartbeat that ends it (`custody-seat.ts`, the raise ledger's writer). E.

!!! THE HOSTED ROAD
* `H1` The operator's answer and the door that shows what waits (`host door`, `host answer`). H.
* `H2` The delegation and three dials stand specified in `hosting-delegation.ts`. Owed: the live issuer, reader, hosting store and socket sorter in one signed-act cut. H.
* `H3` A walker's token buys a knock unless pre-answered (`socket-sorter.ts`). H.
* `H4` The strangers' dial. H.
* `H5` An invited user's root mints on her device, sealed; the herm carries a sealed copy. B.
* `H6` The hosted phone's admission walk: HTTPS, the on-device mint, a QR code or `lar:` URI, a live leaf. Operator's hands. B.
* `H7` One doctrine line still calls an introduction's lifetime unruled (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-invite">>). H, canon.
* `H8` The grant's signed shape and public-half verifier stand specified in `walker-grant.ts` (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember#/the-tiers">>). Owed: the live roll that derives grant public halves for serving rows inside H's one act cut, before E's walker arm. H.

!!! RECOVERY
* Guardian count and threshold remain with the operator (#/open); bundles carry enrolled guardian sets and the restore checks them (#/rulings).
* `V4` The guardian recovery door, the request check, the veto, succession. Operator (#/open). Off this road unless ruled.

!!! THE BROWSER, THE PHONES, TWO HEARTHS
* `B1` Browser custody. The custody API stands specified in `browser-custody.ts`: a passphrase or paper (2-of-3) slot binds the slot tree, the device seed and every Keyhive Archive move into sealed carriers through the mesh's one sealed writer, a wrong route refuses and changes no byte, a locked keystore refuses `sealed-locked` before any mint, and the clear-password act asks through the confirm door and answers only to a literal yes. Owed: the boot unlock and `tm-clear-password` wired in the web boot and `open-browser-vessel.ts`, which also must release its vessel lock on a throw so a `sealed-locked` boot can retry in the same page; the persona roots, which still rest in the clear outside the tree, sealed under it, with the mint refusing until a slot binds (#/rulings); the browser's vessel-key rotation; and the passkey slot, after its derivation gets measured (`B3`) and never alone. Each tab asks for its own unlock, and the ask admits that tab to its face's open hive while the holder keeps a face's keys only while some session of that face stands unlocked (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; the research and its leads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">>). Owed: the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted, its red an unadmitted port that asks for a sealed body and refuses by name; the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive. B.
* `B2` Rung 3: two tabs, two faces, one holder. O1.
* `B3` Device measures owed on the tablet and both phones: owner-kill, the one-tab lock fallback, long background, the passkey derivation and its output across a synced credential's second device, which lifecycle signals reach a page (suspend, OS lock, tab freeze, process kill), eviction over days (`tools/capability-probe/`; the probes read at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">> #/leads-and-probes). Operator's hands. B.
* `B4` QR pairing: the camera road stands unwired, and no decoder dependency or production decode stands. B.
* `B5` The leaf continuity walk (`tools/browser-weld/leaf-continuity.mjs`) drives an offline founding, reload, and Binding Gate fault that must refuse; the admit and join path still lacks a real-browser proof. B.
* `B6` Rung 4: a two-hearth browser walk. X.
* `X1` The automated two-container witness, with no volume in common. X.
* `X2` The ceremony as a walk, in the runbook (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook">>). X.
* `X3` The fresh start by hand on both machines. Operator's hands. X.
* `X4` The parted-authors walk, in the dress rehearsal: two hearths edit one title while apart, rejoin, and each person opens the parallel draft the other left. The walk records whether each recognises their own words and reads why the other version stands live. X.
* `X5` The departure walks, in the dress rehearsal, each on synthetic names and each recording the words the display gives at its incomplete crossing: a wiki closed over a refused save (`G33`); a browser profile reopened on the Archives it kept (`B1`); a public reference followed after its author's vessel went dark (`P10`); a command's outcome read through `lares receipt` after its caller gave up. X.

!!! Carried lanes ~ designed or measured, on no train
* A floor read carries no as-of stamp: `standAs` returns a bare class (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor">>).
* The boot's order holds four named reds nobody wrote, and they gate any split of the boot by region (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/vessel-regions">>).
* The Handle surface adapters: four surfaces stand as type and vocabulary; loopback first, then DNS control (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/handle-card">>). `lares handle graft` stands as a stub over a built mint, where `publish`, `rotate`, `burn` and `attest` run live; the antigen's ban-`nym` move stays untouched; the browser's publish surface and a phone summons that presents the veil card stay owed. Flagged, unbuilt: a Handle's presenting cabal may also serve as its recovery cabal.
* The hostful code half: `carrierBaseRelPath` discards a hostful URI (`bag-paths.ts`), so a hostful title never sites; one carrier claims otherwise (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/lar-uri-namespace">>).
* Title-to-path persistence: the title-to-base map lives in memory alone (`disk-projector.ts`).
* Wikis-first writes: `meme promote` holds no in-wiki path, and the hand-edit weld stays unbuilt, landing last (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology">>).
* Live equivocation's prerequisites: `detectDuplicity` runs in tests alone; no watcher plane, no feed adapter, no durable telemetry (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/live-equivocation">>).
* The crossing record's production membrane around the agent worldline (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/mandate-activity-provenance">>); its two forks read in #/open.
* Whether the browser shore serves its worn face plane, decided against the typed verified-peer seam that stands (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/browser-persona-ring-parity">>).
* Fleet gathering must batch: the one-road delegation cost grows faster than its batch. The petname switcher, the cabal quorum surface for an outward crossing, the browser tier door and the compartment-collector check stand behind it; no live path gathers a fleet yet.
* The self-slot inner ring: it narrows alone, and wiring it freezes a naming (#/open).
* No SES or Compartment realm gate stands in the tree; it gates any live authoring of unpinned code.
* Operator power reaches no browser vessel: a seam enforced by disk access, never a capability. Co-hosted sovereignty between same-uid peers stands claimed and unenforced.
* The crossing rail's three requirements (both ends as presented capabilities, a saga shape, declared deletion semantics) and a realm tally's move onto the shared substrate both stand researched and unbuilt.
* A deny-only antigen share wants entries that can lapse, carried provenance and a merge rule before two lists ever merge.
* Observer-local hardening by silence must BOUND its wait, or a withheld update freezes a victim (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/field-collision">>).
* One charter per vessel rests on a single seal home (`larSealHome`), a guard on one file and never a law; a vessel that carries a second Nexus wants a second seal home, and the charter train names none.
* Realm standing does not cross operators: a feed slot lands in its writer's own daemon bag. The cure points the realm verbs' store at the realm's shared substrate and requires the seal on a foreign slot; the seal verifier holds no caller yet (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/cabal-realm-clock.ts`).
* The bag-tier reader takes the hearth's manifest alone; a repository-homed manifest reads VEIL, tighter and never looser.
* The declared tier's share gate stands specified: `capTierShareDecision` reaches no vessel's share config, and the contract-secrets registry holds no importer (`federation-gate.ts`, `plane-secrets.ts`). A bag's declared tier bites at the crossing gate and the bulb read face alone. The first composer that seats the gate hands its floor oracle all three readings, since an absent secrets reading floors a federatable document public (`cap-tier.ts`).
* A startup module inside the VM, wiring whatever the projection environment lacks, stands held; the off-main-thread engine research may answer it.
* Builds held on purpose, each on the operator's word: the lease cure, the docker partition scenario, WebTransport, the `<<~?` sigil, the SOURCE tiddler.
* Smaller threads: the tombstone and whiteout verb, reserved; Automerge history growth; `lares wiki` subcommands that print for humans alone; an engine-swap reconcile that answered `current` against a stale engine; the NFC assertion at the ingest shore; the parser's retired typed-edge emission plane (`kumu-device.ts`); a `TimeoutNegativeWarning` in e2e runs, unlocalized; the house's register names ahi kā Hawaiian where its documented home reads Māori, and a primary source should settle it.

